 :lesson/sections
 [{:section/type :communication-multiplied
   :section/id 16
   :section/title "Talking about you (all) in Spanish"
   :section/body
   ["In English you singular and you plural is always just you. But in Spanish the distinction is clear. To be clear we'll use the Texas plural - you all."
    "Spanish verbs about you all (second person plural) end in N. Actually it is really easy. All you need to do is add an N to the singular verb like this:"
    "You want You all want Quiere Quieren You need You all need Necesita necesitan You can you all can Puede pueden"]}]
